1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:03,082
Every night, the sky has a story.

2
00:00:03,032 --> 00:00:05,024
AstroLens helps you read it.

3
00:00:05,024 --> 00:00:07,954
Point your phone up, and the stars have names.

4
00:00:07,954 --> 00:00:13,683
Fly a three-D solar system, with real NASA images for every planet.

5
00:00:13,683 --> 00:00:19,933
Watch Earth form across four and a half billion years, and weigh the competing hypotheses.

6
00:00:19,933 --> 00:00:23,852
Then ask where on Earth we should test Moon and Mars hardware.

7
00:00:23,852 --> 00:00:25,245
AstroLens.

8
00:00:25,245 --> 00:00:26,235
Look up.

9
00:00:26,235 --> 00:00:27,498
Understand.
